      "writtenOn": "2021-06-17T12:13:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Can all the files which will be part of the payload be opened by the client and passed as file descriptors?\n\nHere\u0027s a typical layout for payload.img. (When the client passes apex1/apex2/apk/apk\u0027s idsig)\n\n  * gpt header\n  * partition #0\n    * metadata      // generated\n  * partition #1\n    * apex1\n    * apex1\u0027s size  // generated\n  * partition #2\n    * apex2\n    * apex2\u0027s size  // generated\n  * partition #3\n    * apk\n    * zero padding  // generated\n  * partition #4\n    * apk\u0027s idsig file\n  * gpt footer\n\nI\u0027m not sure if the client can open apex files because for now those apexes are \"system\" files. Other generated files belong to the VM instance, so, yeah, they can be opened by the client.\n\nJiyong, what do you think about the client opening those system apex files?",
      "parentUuid": "2f5bbed7_2c0505d9",
      "revId": "540f2dd8a6c91239df0a4dea4a642baa8f2a8dee",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
